{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791537815,"nonce":"luxHFJSUBm4eQT9ScGSzEO5AmCA=","message":"Removed the unconditional 100 ms idle timeout. Work notifications cover typed signal/property writes, CSS/structural changes, drawn changes, invalidate/quit and scheduler additions/cancellation. Timers created while asleep use current elapsed time; manually ticked/offscreen schedulers remain deterministic. Hot reload retains its explicit file-check deadline.\n\nDepends on xwindow 1415c7c (published wake API), hlwindow 4bacd76 (generated Haxe API + native wait integration), and Ash 1f27156 (ash_host_wait/ash_host_resumed through runtime dispatch v8). Older Ash safely retains bounded waits in the adapter; stock HashLink uses native OS-thread wakeups. Latest release HDLL staged in tools/demo/bin and tools/snapshot/bin; Ash libhl.dylib staged atomically.\n\nRegression: IdleWake passes in both interp and hybrid. A background signal updates, a timer created after idle fires after 0.302/0.314 s for a 0.3 s deadline, invalidate draws and quit exits without input. Runtime handoff tests 2/2; runtime-table checks 3/3. macOS native suite: direct wait 19 passed/3 skipped, external pump 20/2. NUC real GNOME Wayland: external pump 18 passed/4 skipped, direct wait 17/5; no failures. Isolated GNOME headless startup timed out before checks; real-session rerun passed.\n\nTreeMotion temporary counter build waited continuously for 13.272 s until its close deadline, with no new loop turn after 5 s. Quiet production hybrid run: CPU 0.00954/0.00821/0.01170%, physical footprint ~200.2 MiB. Prior runs were 193.5-195.8 MiB; do not confuse JIT variability with deterministic savings. Interp settled CPU 0.00069/0.00054%, footprint151.3 MiB. .ashui/memory-comparison/tree-101612/report.json, tree-100919/report.json and tree-wake-counter.log hold details.\n\nSmoke has one pre-existing failing scroll assertion ([45,-15] vs expected first row -45), reproduced using unchanged HEAD source; deterministic timers and remaining smoke checks pass. Track separately.","files":null}]}